    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93218" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάνδᾰλ-ον</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sandal</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				295
			</span></i>; mostly in pl., <i>sandals,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Merc.
				79
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				83
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				139
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				Aeol.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάμβᾰλον</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Eumel.
				13
			</span></i> K., <i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				98
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.267
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Diotim.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a flat fish</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Matro
				<u>Conv.</u>
				76
			</span></i>; also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σανδάλιον</span></b> ,
			identified by <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψῆττα</span>, but
			distinguished from it by <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				1.7
			</span></i>.</div>
